# Line-ending policy for every checkout of this repository.
#
# Measured problem (2026-10-19): a Windows checkout runs with
# `core.autocrlf=true` and therefore writes CRLF into the working tree, while
# the same clone read from WSL/Linux has `core.autocrlf` unset. That git then
# reports every text file as modified even though the index is already all-LF;
# `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` shows that nothing but the line endings differ.
# `* text=auto` makes git normalize on the way into the index and on the way out
# to the comparison, so both sides agree on what "modified" means without
# forcing anybody's editor or checkout style.
#
# Deliberately NOT `eol=lf`: that would rewrite the CRLF files a Windows
# checkout already has, turning the same phantom diff into a real one there.
* text=auto

# Never normalize binary artifacts.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.tgz binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.zst binary
*.gz binary
*.asar binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
